"""
Cycle 92H -- October: design F08 ("win-gate") of the
October improvement round (2026-11-11) -- written as
a live rule.

STATUS LABEL (user order 2026-11-11): NOT VALIDATED
-- installed by user order 2026-11-11. Round
verdict: NO IMPROVEMENT (AUDIT dense-stream win
64.5% vs 70% floor; section 9 / EC22 battery not run
-- screen stopped it). Written from the round's
filed design F08.

PROVENANCE. F08 is the best attempt of the October
improvement round
(fx_research/m5_validation_series/
round_oct_improve_20261111: SLATE.md frozen before
grading; VERDICT_OCT_IMPROVE.md; machinery work/
{stream.py, cells2.py, grade_finalists.py};
grade_oct_improve.json, finalist F08, design
{wH 0, wM 0, wF 0, QH 66.6, QM 11.425,
mult_mode "asc", lam 1.0, cell_key "exp_shsm",
mu 1.0, veto "wgate_0.55"}). The round ran on the
DENSE live stream -- candidates generated from
candles at October's triple (the same R86-form
generator as the ports), not the stored pool the
earlier designs were filed on. Filed lines, dense
stream, cost 2.5 all-in: DISC kept 525, win 63.6%,
net +1,527.28, leftover +23.4%, red weeks 13;
AUDIT kept 138, win 64.5%, net +361.62, leftover
+27.5%, epd 3.00. The incumbent it was graded
against (cycle92h on the same dense stream): DISC
525 / 45.5% / -1,367.65; AUDIT 138 / 42.8% /
-437.37. F08 earned the round's IMPROVED mark on 4
of 5 headline statistics (AUDIT net, AUDIT
leftover, AUDIT win, DISC net; AUDIT epd tied) and
a far better risk arm on drawdown (252.5 vs
1,823.19) and red weeks (13 vs 35), worst pair
worse (-137.7 vs -34.61). It is NOT VALIDATED: the
screen's AUDIT win >= 70% arm is a reality test and
was never waived; zero of the round's 12 finalists
passed it (best 64.5%), so under the locked grading
order the section 9 / EC22 / LCT / DSR battery
never ran. The user ordered this install anyway
(2026-11-11); the round's NO IMPROVEMENT record
stands as written and is not changed by it. 1,407
DISC-fitted designs were tried in the round; F08
was graded once on AUDIT; 2026 was never fitted or
read by the round.

THE RULE (what this module computes at a check
slot). Check slots are the October slots UTC
(15, 17, 18) = 21:30 / 23:30 / 00:30 MMT, October
weekdays only (the app routes month 10 here). At a
slot the module builds candidate trades from the
candles for every one of the 28 symbols: entry at
the close of the M15 bar ending at the slot; M15
ATR14 sets the distance ladder {0.5, 0.75, 1.0,
1.5} x ATR for SL and TP (RR 1:1); exit by the
locked replay (SL-first in one bar, 48h cap). Each
candidate is a (symbol x side x distance-step)
triple keyed to its mined cell (symbol, UTC hour,
side, step). Two DISC-fitted cell tables ship
below as data (fitted on the round's DISC
2016-2023 dense-stream candidates only --
work/cells2.py `build`, shrinkage k=100 toward the
DISC global priors: mean net -2.5662 pips, win
0.4829):

  GATE: a candidate is eligible only if its cell's
  shrunk DISC win rate is >= 0.55 (a cell absent
  from the table reads 0.0 and fails the gate --
  the round's own lookup convention).

  SCORE = the cell's shrunk DISC expectancy (mean
  net pips) + 1.0 x component agreement of the
  entry bar's features (sH, sM, sF):
  agreement = 1 - (|sH-sM| + |sM-sF| + |sH-sF|)/2,
  with sH = clip(0.5 + side * H1drift / (2 * qH),
  0, 1), H1drift the 12-bar H1 drift in pips,
  qH = 66.6; sM the same form over the M15 8-bar
  deviation with qM = 11.425; sF the last M5 bar's
  side-oriented shape (0.5 * loc + 0.25 + 0.25 *
  side * bodyr); undefined features take the
  neutral 0.5. The filed combination weights are
  all zero -- the combination enters F08 only
  through this agreement term.

THE FILL (the filed order, in live form). Per
slot, eligible candidates are ordered by score
descending; ties by step ascending, then the
canonical order (symbol, side desc, step asc).
THE PICK: the first candidate in that order whose
symbol is not blocked by a still-open kept trade
-- exactly one pick per slot; a slot whose
candidates all fail the gate (or are all blocked)
goes unfilled. A kept pick blocks its symbol
until its candle-replayed exit (1-open-per-
symbol); an exit exactly at a slot leaves the
symbol free at that slot, as filed. Single-pick,
as graded.

TRANSLATIONS. The module reuses the October
port's (cycle92h) live machinery unchanged --
candidate generation from candles, the
ATR-step-band exits, the persisted fill ledger --
with F08's gate / score / fill order in place of
the weighted sMC ranking, exactly as the round's
own stream simulator implemented them (the round
verified its candidate outcomes against the port
module's _trade_outcome 384/384 and its fill
against the module's FillState picks 66/66 on Oct
2023). Candidate availability live is
candle-bounded (the frame required a full 192-bar
forward window); the gate's cell tables are
DISC-era data and are never refitted at runtime.
This module has not been proofed beyond the
round's own grading of the design; it is labelled
NOT VALIDATED above and must not be represented
as validated.
"""


